b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING incremental;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for blocks and arrays whose bounds are computed at run time (5.2.4.2), recursive procedures and function designators with value and name parameters (4.7, 5.4) and procedures as actual parameters (4.7.5, 5.4.4), each solution being passed to a parameterless procedure in the way of the procedures passed as parameters in Knuth's man or boy test (1964, examples/man-or-boy-1964.alg in the image), the for statement (4.6) and conditional statements (4.5), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, print, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1) and its own X1 programs cite them (Kruseman Aretz 2003, chapter 7), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), sequences as parallel arrays of heads and tail indices (systems file, Values), and the message loop, spawn message and observe block of the harness README (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.2, 2.6 and the example X01 of 2.8);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS a line 1: L e1 ... eL, the length and then the elements of the known sequence of computation B, rev(that sequence, b). Elements are integers, an atom being its integer code. The harness sends the line after each spawn message of stage 1, so computation A reads it too, and does not use it;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P09a. Two computations, spawned one after the other by the harness, in the instance's spawn order. A: loop(x), by loop's one case, loop(x) if loop(x), a procedure that calls itself, x unknown. B: rev(a, b) with a known, b computed from a by the cases of rev, in order, as a function, the direction this query uses, conc likewise computing its third place from the first two. ALGOL 60 has one computation only, so a spawned computation is a procedure of this program, run to its end before the next message is read. Both share the variables of the outer block. A sequence is a cell index into the arrays hd and tl, 0 being the empty sequence, and a cell c being the sequence hd[c] followed by the sequence tl[c];
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, c, la, xv, loop1, conc1, conc2, rev1, rev2;
  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ xk;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ code := read;
  xk := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;
  loop1 := conc1 := conc2 := rev1 := rev2 := 0;

  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ t̲r̲u̲e̲ d̲o̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: one message, spawn computation c of stage k, and then the stage's constants;
    code := read; k := read; c := read;
    la := read;
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ top, a0, b0;
      i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ hd, tl[1:la + la × (la + 1) ÷ 2 + 1];

      i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ cons(h, t);
        v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ h, t; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ h, t;
      c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ a new cell, the sequence h followed by the sequence t;
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ top := top + 1; hd[top] := h; tl[top] := t; cons := top e̲n̲d̲ cons;

      i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ readseq(len);
        v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ len; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ len;
      c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ a sequence of len elements, read from the input in order;
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j, e, first, last, cl;
        first := last := 0;
        f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ len d̲o̲
        b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
          e := read; cl := cons(e, 0);
          i̲f̲ last = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ first := cl e̲l̲s̲e̲ tl[last] := cl;
          last := cl
        e̲n̲d̲;
        readseq := first
      e̲n̲d̲ readseq;

      i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ conc(a, b);
        v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ a, b; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a, b;
      c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ conc(a, b, c), computing c from a and b by its cases, in order. Case 1: conc(the empty sequence, b, b). Case 2: conc(h followed by a, b, h followed by c) if conc(a, b, c);
      i̲f̲ a = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ conc1 := conc1 + 1; conc := b e̲n̲d̲
      e̲l̲s̲e̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ cc;
        conc2 := conc2 + 1;
        cc := conc(tl[a], b);
        conc := cons(hd[a], cc)
      e̲n̲d̲ conc;

      i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ rev(a);
        v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ a; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a;
      c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ rev(a, b), computing b from a by its cases, in order. Case 1: rev(the empty sequence, the empty sequence). Case 2: rev(h followed by l, r) if rev(l, q) and conc(q, the sequence of h alone, r), its conjuncts in that order;
      i̲f̲ a = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ rev1 := rev1 + 1; rev := 0 e̲n̲d̲
      e̲l̲s̲e̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ q;
        rev2 := rev2 + 1;
        q := rev(tl[a]);
        rev := conc(q, cons(hd[a], 0))
      e̲n̲d̲ rev;

      p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ loop(xk, x, found);
        b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ xk; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ x; p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ found;
      c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ loop(x), by its one case: loop(x) if loop(x). Each solution would be passed to found;
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ loop1 := loop1 + 1; loop(xk, x, found) e̲n̲d̲ loop;

      p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ num(v);
        v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ v; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v;
      c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: an integer, a minus sign if it is negative and then its decimal digits, with no spaces;
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ d;
        i̲f̲ v < 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`-'); num(-v) e̲n̲d̲
        e̲l̲s̲e̲
        b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
          i̲f̲ v ≥ 10 t̲h̲e̲n̲ num(v ÷ 10);
          d := v - v ÷ 10 × 10;
          i̲f̲ d = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`0') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`1') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`2')
          e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`3') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 4 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`4') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 5 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`5')
          e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 6 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`6') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 7 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`7') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 8 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`8')
          e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`9')
        e̲n̲d̲
      e̲n̲d̲ num;

      p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ printseq(p);
        v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ p; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p;
      c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: a sequence, its elements in parentheses, separated by commas;
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j;
        PRINTTEXT(`(');
        f̲o̲r̲ j := 0 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ p ≠ 0 d̲o̲
        b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ num(hd[p]); p := tl[p]; i̲f̲ p ≠ 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ') e̲n̲d̲;
        PRINTTEXT(`)')
      e̲n̲d̲ printseq;

      p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ answera;
      c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: one solution of A, the value of x;
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        PRINTTEXT(`[answer]x');
        i̲f̲ xk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(` = '); num(xv) e̲n̲d̲ e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(` free');
        b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲
      e̲n̲d̲ answera;

      top := 0;
      a0 := readseq(la);

      i̲f̲ c = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ computation A: loop(x), with x unknown;
        loop(xk, xv, answera);
        b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[observe]computation A ended'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
        PRINTTEXT(`[operations loop/1 '); print(loop1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
        b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲
      e̲n̲d̲
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ c = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ computation B: rev(a, b), with a known;
        b0 := rev(a0);
        PRINTTEXT(`[answer]b = '); printseq(b0); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
        b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[observe]computation B ended'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
        PRINTTEXT(`[bind b]'); printseq(b0); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
        PRINTTEXT(`[operations rev/1 '); print(rev1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
        PRINTTEXT(`[operations rev/2 '); print(rev2); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
        PRINTTEXT(`[operations conc/1 '); print(conc1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
        PRINTTEXT(`[operations conc/2 '); print(conc2); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
        b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲
      e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[end]')
  e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
